alabofur (1.1.1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Limits set in alabofur.conf are no longer silently overridden by files
    written by `add`/`deny`; alabofur.conf wins and duplicates are reported.
  * `add` and `deny` update the file that already defines the interface.
  * A missing or failing interface no longer prevents the others from being
    limited, and no half-configured ifb device is left behind.
  * Service: add reload, remove limits on stop, wait for late interfaces and
    use the path of the installed script. Run `alabofur install-service
    --force` after upgrading to refresh the unit.
  * Reject zero limits, accept inline comments in config files.
  * Support interface names longer than 11 characters.
  * Install iproute-tc on Fedora/RHEL, where tc is a separate package.
  * Depend on gawk in the rpm, which minimal openSUSE installs lack.
  * Find tc/ip/modprobe when sbin is not in PATH.

 -- Tuncay Bahadır <tuncaybahadir@protonmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

alabofur (1.1.0) jammy; urgency=medium

  * New `alabofur top` command: live download/upload rate per interface,
    share of the configured limit in use, packets dropped by shaping and
    the processes using the most TCP bandwidth (refreshed every second).
  * The help screen now shows the live rate and configured limit of every
    interface under the logo.

 -- Tuncay Bahadır <tuncaybahadir@protonmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0000

